    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="66377cc8-dc16-5b4a-9486-385c75233de9" activityNameId="27ec605a-97cf-5f4d-bc9b-41e08214d0ed" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Printed wiring board mounting plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Printed wiring board mounting plant
The functional unit represents a production site for the mounting of printed wiring boards, comprising 6 SMT lines and 5 THT lines. Process data based on own estimations, using rough information about Asian plants. The here described plant has an assumed output of 60'000 m2 or 192’000 kg per year over a time span of 25 years.; UUID: 8ccd04f1-817b-33f3-ade4-fc2e43be7196
This module includes land use, buildings and facilities (machinery, cables, etc.) as well as the respective disposal activities of a plant for printed wiring board mounting.
Location: This module relates to the global situation.
Technology: Up-to-date SMT and THT mounting plant, based on information from literature &amp; a plant visit in Switzerland
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: 
Sampling: Literature &amp; own estimations
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_8ccd04f1-817b-33f3-ade4-fc2e43be7196.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
